# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Proprietary reference assemblies — NOT redistributable.
#
# libs/ holds the BepInEx 6 (IL2CPP) framework assemblies and the VRChat /
# Unity / Il2CppInterop interop assemblies. Those are generated from a local
# VRChat install and are Unity's / VRChat's property, so they are never
# committed. See the README for how to produce them into libs/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
libs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Embedded media assets — NOT distributed for licensing reasons.
#
# ressources/ contains audio, fonts, images and pre-baked frame data, some of
# it third-party. The .csproj embeds a subset of these; supply your own (or
# strip the matching <EmbeddedResource> entries) to build. See the README.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ressources/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime capture dumps (may contain instance/user data) and local archives
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
captures/
*.rar
*.7z
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python tooling caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor/perf scratch copies kept beside a file while tuning it — never part of a build.
*.bak-*

# The author's own copy-to-plugins script: hardcoded local drive layout, of no use to
# anyone else and not something a public repo should advertise.
DEPLOY.bat

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only source: real user ids.
#
# *.local.cs holds data about identifiable people (signature sounds are keyed
# by VRChat user id). The publication rule for this repo is that no real user
# id ships in it -- the audit before the first push blanked the ones that had
# reached ModConfig defaults. The partial methods these files implement have
# no body in the public tree, so it compiles with an empty table, the same way
# it compiles without the media in ressources/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.local.cs

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Native (C++) engine build output — cpp/native. Only source is tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
x64/
*.tlog
*.lastbuildstate
*.ipch
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib
